---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Poetry Submissions Directory">
	<main class="about-container">
		<a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Directory</a>
		
		<h1>About SUBtexts</h1>
		
		<div class="content-block">
			<p>This site is not intended to help you send hundreds of submissions to large numbers of magazines indiscriminately. Poetry editors are overworked and underpaid, and vitally, pivotally important to our poetry scene. Please respect them by reading submission guidelines very carefully, and by submitting only to magazines which you've carefully selected as being appropriate for your work. Wherever you can, please consider buying the magazines you're interested in submitting to. </p>

			<p>Next, a disclaimer. I'm ultimately hoping that this site will become accurate through crowd-sourcing, but at the moment the info is a bit patchy, and there will definitely be mistakes. Currently, submissions beinng open or closed is updated dynamically using basic AI tools (I know. I don't like it either). The fact that this doesn't work perfectly is really on me, although it's also true that poetry magazines are *terrible* at providing structured information about when they're accepting submissions. The statuses (Open, Closed, Soon) are checked roughly once a week, in rolling daily batches of forty. But please don't take any of this as gospel.</p>			
			<p>I know the 'prestige' metric is a wild choice, but I've found a lot of poets starting out are very intimidated by the sheer number of publications, and find it hard to discern what's read widely and what's not. This is some hopeless attempt to communicate that information. It's probably innacurate, but the good news is that you can at least contribute to the score by voting <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSegWBNVct1rpCaY3BprNLi_fa5G9Ma1QZNi4akJoaJ_4PzweA/viewform?usp=dialog">here</a>. Please don't try and game the system, take offence, or otherwise freak out. I am doing my best.</p>
			<p>If you run a magazine and need your details updated, or if you spot an error – or if you'd like to help out, or if you have ideas of how to improve things – please feel free to email me on poetrysubssite@gmail.com.</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-container {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3rem 0;
	}

	.back-link {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		color: #555;
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.back-link:hover {
		color: #000;
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	p, li {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #333;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
</style>